 "notes": [
  "end: the still sequence stops at t=104.03 s with the flame still burning (117 frames shot per the table, 100 on the proof sheet). The duct view follows the tip to t=114.25 s (x=0.2 of the frame, with a gap) where it is lost in noise; at that x the T5 flame reached the window end, so the T6 flame most likely reached the downstream end of the window.",
  "time: t_s = overlay-clock seconds after igniter-off. Igniter-off = steepest drop of the igniter-box brightness in the duct video (frame resolution) at video 10.24 s; igniter-on = first frame with the box 99th-percentile red >= dark + 20 at video 4.57 s. Overlay clock from the whole-second readings by local interval intersection (+-15 s), half-width 0.24 s at igniter-off.",
  "stills: camera stamps are whole seconds; times use a local cadence reconstruction (+-8 neighbouring stamps, their first-to-last cadence; mean cadence 1.1313 s): 74/100 stills placed inside the intersection of their neighbours' whole-second intervals (median interval width 0.12 s), the rest at stamp + 0.5 s. clock.still_minus_overlay_s = camera clock minus overlay clock from the brackets: igniter onset between stills at camera 29.83 and 30.95 s-of-minute (overlay onset 30.81), igniter light gone between stills 35.50 and 36.57 (overlay off 36.48); onset bracket [-0.98, 0.14], off bracket [-0.98, 0.08] s; intersection of the onset and off brackets. Exposure length is unknown and not included.",
  "position: x_w = (x_up - x_px)/band_width_px in the 324x216 proof-sheet thumbnails. x_up = 306.3 px = right (igniter-side) edge of the lit band and coil, half-maximum of the green channel in the dimmest igniter-lit still (#4); repeatability across tests about +-3 px (0.05 w) because the coil glare sets this edge. 1 px = 0.0180 w. tip_w from the left (downstream) edge of the largest blue region, base_w from its right (upstream) edge.",
  "quality: edge = region touches the picture border, the base is within 1 px of x_up (anchored at the igniter end), or the tip within 1 px of the window end; weak = area < 200 px or blue sum < 12000 (dim); else ok. area_px and blue_sum are extra per-still fields (largest blue region, 324x216 px, background-subtracted blue sum).",
  "duct: 1-s window track from the earlier analysis (brightness R+G+B, z>4, dilated, detection threshold 1.5x dark-null maximum); tip_fw = left (downstream) end, base_fw = right (upstream) end, in fractions of the 720-px frame registered to the overlay (FUEL label at 166 px); x DECREASES downstream. area_px, signal are extra per-window fields. Duct is a second view, not converted to w here.",
  "fan: displayed FAN after a 3-sample (1.5 s) running median of the 0.5-s overlay readings (removes single misreads and single-sample 41/42 flicker); u_cm_s = 1.0066 x AIR interpolated linearly in that day's 2-restrictor calibration rows, null below the lowest non-zero row (sheet advises against the zero-flow row).",
  "table: Fan display column = '', Total Frames Shot = 117, radiometer gain 50, CO2 0.24 -> 0.28 %, CO 39 -> 77 ppm, date 4/10/2014 (video display is one day later).",
  "geometry: the T6 band is not lit to its downstream end in the igniter stills (red-channel rise found at [] px, dim), so window_length_w is null. If the T5/T16 framing applies (downstream end 54.0/53.7 px), the window length would be about 4.54 w [assumption]."
